 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Affineness is insensitive to thickenings",
 "statement": "Let i_S:S⟶S' and i_X:X⟶X' be thickenings, and let f':X'⟶S' and f:X⟶S commute with them. If f is affine, then f' is affine.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/more-morphisms.tex",
  "place": "More on Morphisms, Lemma 09ZV (1), using Lemma 06AD"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sbc-first-order-thickening",
  "pqf-def-affine-morphism"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Let V be an affine open of S′. Closed immersions are affine, so i_S⁻¹(V) is affine; affineness of f gives affineness of f⁻¹(i_S⁻¹(V)). By the commuting square this equals i_X⁻¹(f′⁻¹(V)). Restrict i_X to f′⁻¹(V). It remains a closed immersion and is surjective: each point has a lift under i_X and that lift belongs to the preimage open. It is therefore a thickening whose source is affine. Apply isAffine_of_isThickening (Stacks 06AD) to get affineness of f′⁻¹(V). Since V was arbitrary, f′ is affine.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-weil-pbc-thickening-affine-scheme",
    "lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-integral-separated-uc"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
